# Example CODEOWNERS entry for the threat model file.
# Copy the relevant line(s) into your repository's .github/CODEOWNERS and set the team/user.
#
# This makes a security reviewer a required approver whenever the model file changes (combine
# with a branch protection rule that requires code owner review — see guide/ci-integration.md).
#
# Note: GitHub cannot restrict *who* may apply a PR label beyond "triage" repo permission or
# above. The `skip-label` used by the threat-model gate (default: threat-model-not-needed) is
# NOT enforced by CODEOWNERS — restrict who gets triage/write access, or treat the label as a
# social/process control, not a technical one.

threat-model/project.json         @your-org/security-reviewers

# A pull_request workflow runs the PR's own version of the workflow file, so a PR could remove
# the gate by editing it. Put the workflow (and custom trigger definitions, if any) under the
# same reviewers.
.github/workflows/threat-model.yml  @your-org/security-reviewers
# threat-model/triggers.yaml        @your-org/security-reviewers
